    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4980",
      "problem": "The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below. Sketch the graph of $y=4f(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218586/assets/495e5e02f89dfa125cb95095088cb80cf3e83ab9e6dae619494e900cbe1dc346.png)",
      "worked_solution": "To graph the function $y = 4f(x),$ we take the graph of $y = f(x)$ and stretch it by factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y = f(x)$ by $4.$\n\nThe resulting graph is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218586/assets/0b20c1355ae0b2e8afc7e7ce701662e0aaf2a6fdcd8e43342ae057e8bd9250e9.png)",
